# Quadratic equations

Today we solve equations of the form $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$ where $a \neq 0$.

::: definition Quadratic equation
A **quadratic equation** is a polynomial equation of degree 2.
:::

::: theorem Quadratic formula {key}
$$ x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} $$
:::

The number $\Delta = b^2 - 4ac$ is the *discriminant*. It tells us how many real roots there are.

| $\Delta$ | real roots |
|---|---|
| $\Delta > 0$ | two |
| $\Delta = 0$ | one |
| $\Delta < 0$ | none |

::: example
Solve $x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0$.
Solution:
$$
x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0
(x - 2)(x - 3) = 0
$$
So $x = 2$ or $x = 3$.
:::

